        "id": 1305927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-07-28T15:24:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Storm tracking stops the interrupts to prevent the EC from watchdogging. The current patchset of this CL disables storm tracking entirely, which means that interrupts will never be disabled during a BIST test. But, since the test passes, clearly the EC did not watchdog.\n\nThat implies that there exist values of `ALERT_STORM_INTERVAL` and `ALERT_STORM_MAX_COUNT` that would allow the test to pass _and_ not allow the EC to watchdog, at least on this board. Maybe we need to make the value board-specific, but that would be preferable to just disabling the storm tracker mechanism entirely during a BIST test (effectively setting `ALERT_STORM_MAX_COUNT` to infinity).\n\nI\u0027m asking you to figure out what value of `ALERT_STORM_MAX_COUNT` will allow the test to pass while still preventing the EC from watchdogging at higher interrupt rates than those seen in the test.",
      "parentUuid": "a60997ec_e1509179",
      "revId": "3d71ad3dc69839850dc52f43d5d01de130cdbe47",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
